  <!-- Section 5: How to Verify Ethical Claims -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">How to Verify a Manufacturer's Ethical Claims</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Verifying ethical claims is essential because unsubstantiated ethical statements are meaningless. Many manufacturers claim to be "ethical" without third-party verification, making it impossible for brands to assess actual labor practices. Genuine ethical manufacturers provide certification numbers, audit reports, and verification links that enable brands to independently verify compliance. This section provides a step-by-step process for verifying ethical manufacturing claims and identifying genuine versus deceptive claims.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        The verification process begins with requesting certification numbers for all claimed certifications. BSCI certificates can be verified through the amfori database at amfori.org. WRAP certificates can be verified through the WRAP database at wrapcompliance.org. Fair Trade certificates can be verified through Fair Trade International at fairtrade.net. Always verify certificate validity dates and ensure the factory name matches the certificate holder. Fraudulent certificates exist in the market, so direct verification through official databases is essential.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Beyond certificate verification, request current audit reports showing compliance scores and any corrective actions required. Audit reports provide detailed evidence of factory performance across specific criteria. Look for audit dates within the past 12 months - certifications older than this may not reflect current conditions. Ask for evidence of fair wage payments, working hour records, and safety incident reports. Genuine ethical manufacturers provide this documentation willingly and transparently.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Ethical Verification Checklist</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        Use this checklist to systematically verify manufacturer ethical claims. Complete verification across all items provides confidence in genuine ethical production.
